      "body": "### Project URL\n\nhttps://github.com/Omibranch/gitty\n\n### Category\n\nGo\n\n### Project Title\n\nSingle-binary Git+GitHub CLI wrapper that condenses git workflow into one command\n\n### Project Description\n\ngitty is a minimal, single-binary CLI tool written in Go that wraps git and GitHub CLI into short, human-readable commands. The star feature is \\`gitty up\\` which replaces the entire \\`git add → git commit → git push\\` cycle with one command. Also supports: \\`gitty fix <file>\\` for interactive conflict resolution, \\`gitty erase <path>\\` to permanently remove paths from all past commits, \\`gitty pick file.go 10-20\\` for selective line-range commits, and \\`gitty back N\\` to undo the last N commits. Runs on Linux (amd64/arm64), macOS, and Windows as a single zero-dependency binary.\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Zero dependencies: single binary install via curl, yay (Arch), or winget (Windows)\n- Replaces multiple git commands with one memorable command (\\`gitty up\\`)\n- Supports GitHub-specific features (share repo, rename, delete via GitHub CLI)\n- Written in Go: fast, cross-platform, low memory footprint\n\n### Example Code\n\n\\`\\`\\`bash\n# Instead of: git add -A && git commit -m '...' && git push\ngitty up\n\n# With a custom commit message\ngitty up \"feat: add login page\"\n\n# Fix a merge conflict interactively\ngitty fix src/main.go\n\n# Remove a file from ALL past commits (git history rewrite)\ngitty erase secrets.env\n\n# Commit only lines 10-20 of a specific file\ngitty pick src/main.go 10-20\n\\`\\`\\`",
